1
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:05,045
- Careful with the stroller.
- Yes, boss.

2
00:00:05,046 --> 00:00:07,381
She loves these. Don't drop them.

3
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,342
Please give my daughter back.

4
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:15,473
What are you talking about? Your daughter?

5
00:00:22,188 --> 00:00:25,023
I left my daughter
outside your door last week.

6
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,568
Please give her back.

7
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:34,825
That's not true.

8
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:35,951
Leave now,

9
00:00:35,952 --> 00:00:37,412
or I won't be so nice.

10
00:00:38,538 --> 00:00:42,458
I know you lost your baby,
but I can't be without my daughter either.

11
00:00:42,459 --> 00:00:44,753
- Please give her back--
- Stop this nonsense.

12
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,421
Damn. Get this crazy woman out.

13
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,298
You can't bully me
because you're gangsters.

14
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:50,591
Give her back!

15
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:52,259
- Ruyi! Brother Xiao!
- Move!

16
00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:53,302
Don't hurt her.

17
00:00:53,303 --> 00:00:54,679
I'm sorry, Brother Xiao.

18
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:02,062
She's your girlfriend?

19
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,023
Then the baby...

20
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:08,485
Brother Xiao, I'll explain later.

21
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:10,612
Just give her a chance.

22
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,989
Can you give Taozi back?

23
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,202
Looks like he won't.

24
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:24,291
Not funny.

25
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:25,752
I'm sorry.

26
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,712
- Give her back! Taozi's inside!
- Ruyi!

27
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:30,965
- I'll go get her back.
- Only Little Rice Cake's here.

28
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,384
Honey.

29
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:36,095
I don't care what happened before.

30
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:39,056
Listen to me, and listen carefully.

31
00:01:39,057 --> 00:01:41,059
Only Little Rice Cake is here.

32
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:43,019
I never want to see her again.

33
00:01:44,270 --> 00:01:45,313
Get her out.

34
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:36,864
Let go!

35
00:02:36,865 --> 00:02:39,783
Ruyi, can you calm down?

36
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:41,076
I'm getting Taozi back.

37
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,203
There's no point going now.

38
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:45,080
I told you, I'll find a way.

39
00:02:45,081 --> 00:02:47,541
You knew he had Taozi.
Now you're a coward?

40
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:50,544
Going now won't make them give Taozi back.

41
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:53,714
After what happened,
I don't know what Brother Xiao might do.

42
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:55,132
He pointed a gun at me.

43
00:02:55,133 --> 00:02:57,342
If they hurt me, I'll call the cops.

44
00:02:57,343 --> 00:02:58,886
The cops won't help.

45
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,512
Brother Xiao has connections.

46
00:03:00,513 --> 00:03:04,057
I'll tell the police.
A DNA test can prove Taozi is my daughter.

47
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,143
Then what?

48
00:03:05,935 --> 00:03:10,063
You gave Taozi away first,
and you don't have a steady income.

49
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:11,733
Social services might take her.

50
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:21,659
Ruyi,

51
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:24,162
I'll get Taozi back.

52
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:27,165
I promise.

53
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,092
Honey,

54
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:41,179
when did you find out?

55
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,849
After being in the ICU for so long,

56
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:46,935
I already suspected it.

57
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:57,904
Did you give her a proper send-off?

58
00:03:59,822 --> 00:04:01,032
Of course I did.

59
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:04,077
I said goodbye to her properly.

60
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:08,872
You're not mad I hid it, right?

61
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:10,583
I failed her.

62
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:13,670
I couldn't give birth to her safely.

63
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:16,296
Don't say that.

64
00:04:16,297 --> 00:04:18,549
You can't blame yourself
for what happened.

65
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,053
I know grieving

66
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:24,681
won't bring our daughter back.

67
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,850
But heaven took pity on me

68
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:32,814
and sent us this adorable baby
in her place.

69
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,859
I'll be a good mother.

70
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:39,404
We're a family now.

71
00:04:40,405 --> 00:04:42,323
I can't lose another child.

72
00:04:43,741 --> 00:04:45,326
Honey, you have to help me.

73
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:48,705
Absolutely.

74
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,339
That's too much.

75
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,676
How can they just keep Taozi
for themselves?

76
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,554
We've watched her grow up.

77
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:06,973
If she grows up like this,

78
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:09,350
won't she become a big-time gangster?

79
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:15,731
Here's what I'm thinking.

80
00:05:15,732 --> 00:05:18,860
If we can't take her by force,
why don't we sneak her out?

81
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:22,155
Brother Xiao and Sister Zhuzhu know us,

82
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:24,949
so we can't show up.

83
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:28,660
If we can't show up,
who'll bring Taozi back?

84
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:30,830
You'll just have to rely on their help.

85
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:33,791
Us?

86
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:37,336
Me too.

87
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,799
I have an idea.

88
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,594
I'll make a call.

89
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:47,555
I was thinking maybe you two could...

90
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:09,660
Zhuzhu, isn't she too bundled up?

91
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:13,331
Didn't you hear Little Rice Cake
sneezing nonstop earlier?

92
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:18,543
The doctor said too many layers
can give a baby heatstroke.

93
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:20,588
Go make me a bottle of formula.

94
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:23,173
Another bottle?

95
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:26,385
She just finished one.
You want another already?

96
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:29,971
She needs to eat more to gain weight.

97
00:06:29,972 --> 00:06:31,306
Go make the bottle.

98
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:34,227
- Don't overfeed her.
- Just go!

99
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:36,686
Okay, I'll go.

100
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:41,233
You, how many times do I have to tell you?
Look carefully. That's not the right one!

101
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,859
- Not this one?
- In the kitchen.

102
00:06:42,860 --> 00:06:44,237
The one for her stomach.

103
00:06:45,071 --> 00:06:48,198
If we don't get Taozi out,
she'll die young like us.

104
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:51,035
Isn't it too soon?
What are those two doing? Hurry up!

105
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,454
Isn't it all the same?

106
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,041
Who's this?

107
00:06:58,042 --> 00:07:00,127
Hello, this is the health center.

108
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:03,923
Your child is due
for a hepatitis B vaccine.

109
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:08,552
Zhuzhu, the health center says
the baby needs a hepatitis B shot.

110
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:11,264
Strange, the doctor
didn't mention it yesterday.

111
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:14,767
We'll go another day.

112
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:18,228
Hello? We'll come another day.

113
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:19,439
Now what? It failed.

114
00:07:20,356 --> 00:07:25,152
Sir, there have been
a lot of hepatitis B cases lately.

115
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,445
<i>- Some are severe.</i>
- Now what?

116
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,029
<i>- Some even died.</i>
- Get him!

117
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:29,739
<i>- Vaccines are few.</i>
- Get him!

118
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,535
<i>Come tomorrow for the vaccine,
just to be safe.</i>

119
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,496
- That serious?
- Damn, you scared me!

120
00:07:36,581 --> 00:07:37,623
Brother Xiao.

121
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,208
Brother Xiao.

122
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:59,311
Uncle and Auntie here?

123
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:00,520
Yeah, don't worry.

124
00:08:00,521 --> 00:08:02,190
Uncle's working hard.

125
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,616
It's weird seeing you like this.

126
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:14,202
Didn't we need disguises?

127
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:21,750
Brother Xiao won't recognize me.

128
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:23,002
I agree.

129
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,718
What is it? What's wrong?

130
00:08:31,302 --> 00:08:32,469
Honey?

131
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:34,597
I think there's a car following us.

132
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,100
Really?

133
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,575
Why do you have it so easy?

134
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:57,410
No, my skirt's too tight.

135
00:08:57,411 --> 00:08:59,914
I need to stay with Taozi
and keep an eye on her.

136
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:03,793
She smiled!

137
00:09:04,794 --> 00:09:06,754
So cute.

138
00:09:08,464 --> 00:09:10,007
Nice car.

139
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,846
- Be careful.
- Okay.

140
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:24,021
Hurry...

141
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,399
Over here!

142
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:31,152
- We can't let...
- Quick...

143
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:32,654
Where are we going?

144
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:33,989
The engine's still on!

145
00:09:33,990 --> 00:09:36,075
Robbers leave the engine running.

146
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:39,494
Why so long? They said it'd be quick.

147
00:09:39,495 --> 00:09:41,163
Hang on a little longer.

148
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:49,462
Don't sneeze near the baby!

149
00:09:49,463 --> 00:09:50,714
Go somewhere else.

150
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:53,342
Seriously, these people...

151
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,844
Tell them to back off.

152
00:09:55,845 --> 00:09:57,304
Move farther away.

153
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,723
Go over there.

154
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:01,766
Come on.

155
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:02,727
Little Rice Cake!

156
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:06,188
What?

157
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:07,857
That's strange.

158
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,318
Go!

159
00:10:13,821 --> 00:10:17,199
Nerd, no! You'll die!

160
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:20,202
I'll leave it to you guys.

161
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,057
Watch the kid, okay?

162
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:43,683
What just happened?

163
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:46,102
It's okay. Masks are required here.

164
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,395
- Okay.
- Don't worry.

165
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:48,730
- Thank you so much.
- Who is she?

166
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:49,815
Probably a volunteer.

167
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,579
What is this thing?

168
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:07,583
Quick!

169
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:10,002
Hurry, hurry!

170
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,838
- A-Li, I knew it.
- Brother Xiao.

171
00:11:13,839 --> 00:11:14,964
No, Xiao!

172
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:16,383
Brother Xiao, don't!

173
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,259
- Give me Little Rice Cake.
- You win.

174
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:20,136
I'm done with the organization.

175
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:21,430
Give her to me.

176
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:46,204
It's okay.

177
00:11:46,205 --> 00:11:48,499
You're okay. Don't be scared.

178
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,012
Where's Taozi?

179
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:03,764
Where are we?

180
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:07,934
Chang Ruyi.

181
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,186
Li Zhuzhu.

182
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:19,320
Give... Give her back to me.

183
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:21,197
Why is Taozi with you?

184
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:24,075
I'm Peng Ying, the Birth Deity's aide.

185
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:27,120
Great. You know Taozi's
my daughter, right?

186
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,455
Can I have her back?

187
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:29,706
Then...

188
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:33,334
Then you must've seen
that she abandoned her child too.

189
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:36,087
She left her newborn
outside my hospital room.

190
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:37,547
You saw that, right?

191
00:12:37,548 --> 00:12:39,048
I didn't mean to. I was sick.

192
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:40,633
I had postpartum depression.

193
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:43,094
- I didn't mean to--
- Lots of moms get it.

194
00:12:43,095 --> 00:12:45,723
Who abandons their child?
That was irresponsible.

195
00:12:46,432 --> 00:12:47,600
Chang Ruyi!

196
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:50,227
Postpartum depression is no excuse.

197
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,604
I know it's no excuse.

198
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:55,064
I really love her.
Can you give her back to me?

199
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:58,610
I'm not related to this child,
but I'd give my life to protect her.

200
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,944
I love her more.

201
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:02,530
Enough. It doesn't matter
who gave birth to her.

202
00:13:02,531 --> 00:13:07,202
I'm going to decide who's most qualified
to be this child's mother.

203
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:12,040
Whoever convinces me gets the child.

204
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:14,627
Li Zhuzhu, you go first.

205
00:13:21,133 --> 00:13:22,468
I prayed for years

206
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,013
to have a child

207
00:13:27,556 --> 00:13:30,017
<i>and went through
more than a dozen rounds of IVF.</i>

208
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:32,060
<i>I failed again and again,</i>

209
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:35,231
<i>but I never gave up.</i>

210
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:40,193
<i>Whenever I heard about some remedy
that worked or some great doctor,</i>

211
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,695
<i>I'd try it.</i>

212
00:13:42,655 --> 00:13:46,242
<i>I took every chance I could
to get pregnant.</i>

213
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,329
Finally,

214
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:53,916
I conceived my Little Rice Cake.

215
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:56,418
For the first three months,

216
00:13:57,628 --> 00:14:00,839
<i>I had to stay in the hospital on bed rest.</i>

217
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:04,551
<i>After I was discharged,
I still needed rehab,</i>

218
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:07,388
but it was all worth it.

219
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:12,726
I spent ten months
terrified something might happen.

220
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:16,272
I finally made it to full term.

221
00:14:17,439 --> 00:14:18,273
I thought...

222
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:19,900
On the delivery table,

223
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:22,069
I thought

224
00:14:23,404 --> 00:14:24,488
my...

225
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:29,743
My suffering was finally over
and I'd finally meet my Little Rice Cake.

226
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:34,748
<i>But I never imagined that,</i>

227
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,004
at the very last moment,

228
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,548
my baby would be gone.

229
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:45,885
Just gone.

230
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:51,598
I just don't understand.

231
00:14:51,599 --> 00:14:57,646
If Heaven really decided to take my baby,
why didn't it take me too?

232
00:15:01,942 --> 00:15:04,320
Now that Heaven
has given me another chance,

233
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:07,113
I won't waste it.

234
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:09,157
I'll protect this baby

235
00:15:09,158 --> 00:15:11,409
and love her
just like my Little Rice Cake.

236
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:13,703
I promise I'll be
the best mother I can be.

237
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:14,872
Wait.

238
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:16,831
Look,

239
00:15:16,832 --> 00:15:18,584
Yan Xiaotian,

240
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:22,212
let me ask you.

241
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,548
Did your wife really go through that much
to have a baby?

242
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:27,800
Honey, she's the Birth Deity's aide.

243
00:15:27,801 --> 00:15:30,888
Tell her how much I suffered
to have a baby.

244
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:37,144
Every time my wife's

245
00:15:39,438 --> 00:15:40,730
fertility treatment failed,

246
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:43,692
<i>she'd hide in the bathroom and cry
so I wouldn't know.</i>

247
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:48,655
<i>And her stomach was covered
in injection bruises.</i>

248
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:50,658
<i>And they made her nauseous and sick.</i>

249
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:54,536
<i>I can't count how many times I begged</i>

250
00:15:55,329 --> 00:15:56,454
<i>Heaven to let me,</i>

251
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:59,416
- Yan Xiaotian, suffer in her place.
- All right!

252
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,587
Your turn, Chang Ruyi.

253
00:16:04,755 --> 00:16:07,799
What makes you qualified to be her mother?

254
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,344
I never thought I'd get pregnant.

255
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:13,555
Of course,

256
00:16:14,348 --> 00:16:16,350
I didn't go through as much as she did.

257
00:16:19,019 --> 00:16:23,314
But during my pregnancy,
my body changed and I lost my job.

258
00:16:23,315 --> 00:16:27,610
Later, while breastfeeding,
I got mastitis and ended up in the ER.

259
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,780
I've been through all that, too.

260
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,282
I lost my baby
and still had to recover from postpartum.

261
00:16:33,283 --> 00:16:35,577
Can you imagine that pain?

262
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,663
Have you suffered like I have?

263
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,499
You can't compare motherhood.

264
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:45,295
Everyone's circumstances are different.

265
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,548
To give my child a better life,

266
00:16:48,549 --> 00:16:51,010
<i>I went back to work
before I'd even recovered.</i>

267
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:54,095
No matter how tired,

268
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:57,141
<i>hungry, miserable or sleepy I was
when I got home,</i>

269
00:16:58,017 --> 00:17:01,311
<i>even when washing bottles
left my hands cracked and raw,</i>

270
00:17:02,312 --> 00:17:04,605
the moment I saw her lying in bed,

271
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:06,942
all clean and sweet-smelling,

272
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:10,738
I knew

273
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:13,157
it was all worth it.

274
00:17:13,866 --> 00:17:14,950
Liar.

275
00:17:16,243 --> 00:17:19,037
You gave her up because it was too hard.

276
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,164
I'm not lying.

277
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:23,583
I was afraid she'd end up
like my little sister,

278
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:25,918
unable to grow up safe and healthy

279
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:28,714
<i>because of one careless mistake I made.</i>

280
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,633
But I truly regret it now.

281
00:17:32,634 --> 00:17:34,845
Please, can you give Taozi back to me?

282
00:17:35,596 --> 00:17:36,597
Wait.

283
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:40,975
Tseng Yu-Li, do you think Chang Ruyi

284
00:17:40,976 --> 00:17:42,478
can be a good mother?

285
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:49,026
I don't know.

286
00:17:51,236 --> 00:17:54,448
I don't know
what makes someone a good mother.

287
00:17:57,659 --> 00:17:59,828
When I met Ruyi,

288
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,623
she was a first-time mom

289
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,583
with all the struggles that come with it.

290
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:08,628
At first, she was completely overwhelmed.

291
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,589
When the baby cried, she'd cry too.

292
00:18:11,715 --> 00:18:14,343
But she worked so hard to overcome it all.

293
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:19,640
She sacrificed almost everything
for her child.

294
00:18:20,682 --> 00:18:22,518
She really did.

295
00:18:23,727 --> 00:18:27,481
If that's part of becoming a good mother,

296
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,485
then she's trying incredibly hard
to learn.

297
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:33,946
So please

298
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:37,407
don't take away her chance to learn.

299
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,620
And one last thing.

300
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:47,084
Raising a child alone is just too hard.

301
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:49,627
I'm willing...

302
00:18:49,628 --> 00:18:52,256
I'm willing to help her
take care of Taozi.

303
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,013
All right.

304
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:05,101
Miss Birth Deity's aide, hear me out.

305
00:19:05,102 --> 00:19:08,396
With us, she'll have a mom, a dad,
money and everything she needs.

306
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:10,231
She'll have a happy life.

307
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:12,066
I don't have much money,

308
00:19:12,067 --> 00:19:13,651
but I'll work hard.

309
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:16,529
I really love her.
I can't live without her.

310
00:19:16,530 --> 00:19:18,197
Please give her back to me.

311
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,032
Liar. You abandoned her.

312
00:19:20,033 --> 00:19:22,870
- You'd never protect her.
- No, I would.

313
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:33,463
Taozi.

314
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:35,757
Chang Ruyi,

315
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,135
it seems

316
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:40,929
Li Zhuzhu

317
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:44,099
is better suited
to be this child's mother.

318
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:49,395
Taozi...

319
00:19:49,396 --> 00:19:50,522
Taozi.

320
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:53,275
Give her back.

321
00:19:54,526 --> 00:19:56,153
Where did you go?

322
00:19:57,279 --> 00:19:58,322
<i>Chang Ruyi,</i>

323
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:02,784
<i>I've given you so many chances
and helped you so many times,</i>

324
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:05,037
<i>but you let me down in the end.</i>

325
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,498
<i>I remember you said</i>

326
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,210
<i>at the beginning that you didn't want</i>

327
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:14,796
<i>to get married or be a mother, right?</i>

328
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:16,882
<i>Don't worry.</i>

329
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:19,592
<i>You'll forget what Taozi looks like.</i>

330
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,470
Oh, my God!

331
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:25,682
My Taozi. Give her back.

332
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:31,146
Give her back!

333
00:20:49,414 --> 00:20:52,626
<i>My life has gotten better over the years.</i>

334
00:20:55,128 --> 00:20:56,546
<i>I have a great job</i>

335
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:59,633
<i>and a home of my own.</i>

336
00:21:05,138 --> 00:21:06,055
Ladies,

337
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:08,432
our boss just brought this back
from Korea.

338
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:10,435
<i>But for some reason,</i>

339
00:21:11,895 --> 00:21:13,771
<i>I feel like I've forgotten something.</i>

340
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:17,316
Everyone, this year's sales
are counting on...

341
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:18,735
Ruyi!

342
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:20,695
Sorry.

343
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:22,280
Thanks for all your hard work.

344
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:24,199
- Please help me out.
- Keep it up!

345
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:32,748
I want to make money and be a boss.

346
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:34,376
Love? No way!

347
00:21:42,050 --> 00:21:43,135
Miss?

348
00:21:45,262 --> 00:21:47,638
This is information
about our Taekwondo classes.

349
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:49,974
If you're interested, you can... Miss?

350
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:52,601
Ruyi, didn't you say
you were buying a house?

351
00:21:52,602 --> 00:21:55,188
- You really bought one?
- Yeah, I really did.

352
00:21:56,815 --> 00:22:00,527
Single life is great.
But I pay the mortgage alone.

353
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,653
Here you go.

354
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,071
Thanks.

355
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:05,781
This is really good. You like it?

356
00:22:05,782 --> 00:22:07,533
My favorite candy.

357
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:09,243
Your favorite candy?

358
00:22:09,244 --> 00:22:11,287
Where do you work?

359
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:14,791
I work in fashion retail, doing sales.

360
00:22:15,417 --> 00:22:16,792
What about you?

361
00:22:16,793 --> 00:22:18,045
I work in sales.

362
00:22:32,934 --> 00:22:35,061
Send me the originals when they're ready.

363
00:22:35,062 --> 00:22:36,145
- Okay, thanks.
- Thank you.

364
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:37,647
- I'm so happy.
- Take care.

365
00:22:39,441 --> 00:22:40,608
Keep in touch.

366
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:43,778
Ruyi, could you check this contract?

367
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:45,113
Well...

368
00:22:46,531 --> 00:22:48,575
We need to contact him again about this.

369
00:22:55,540 --> 00:22:57,958
You'll get your milk soon. It's okay.

370
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,003
There, there.

371
00:23:01,713 --> 00:23:03,130
Let me help you.

372
00:23:03,131 --> 00:23:04,090
Thank you.

373
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:06,383
- It's okay. Babies cry.
- Mommy's here.

374
00:23:06,384 --> 00:23:07,593
It's okay now.

375
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:09,346
It's okay.

376
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,224
You're okay.

377
00:23:14,267 --> 00:23:15,602
Can I touch her?

378
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,860
A pretty lady's touching you.

379
00:23:24,861 --> 00:23:26,738
Mommy will make you some milk.

380
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:43,565
Look,

381
00:24:44,816 --> 00:24:47,986
you went through so much
to become a mother,

382
00:24:48,862 --> 00:24:50,404
yet you quickly found

383
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:53,742
another child to replace Little Rice Cake.

384
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,746
But in Chang Ruyi's heart,

385
00:24:58,705 --> 00:24:59,789
no one

386
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,376
could ever replace Taozi.

387
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,296
I've seen how

388
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,924
you've cared for Taozi all this time.

389
00:25:10,634 --> 00:25:14,679
You were anxious, on edge and unhappy.

390
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:19,517
Taozi had a hard time
growing up with you, too.

391
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:24,773
If this continues,
she won't be happy when she grows up.

392
00:25:31,196 --> 00:25:32,572
How can I...

393
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:36,910
have a child of my own?

394
00:25:44,209 --> 00:25:45,210
You can.

395
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,214
Come here.

396
00:25:53,593 --> 00:25:55,262
Every mother and child

397
00:25:56,805 --> 00:25:58,515
are brought together by fate.

398
00:26:00,225 --> 00:26:01,600
If it isn't meant to be,

399
00:26:01,601 --> 00:26:03,270
don't force it.

400
00:26:05,313 --> 00:26:07,314
Since blood ties don't matter to you,

401
00:26:07,315 --> 00:26:10,318
you can give your love
to many more children someday.

402
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:17,075
But there's still one thing
you need to do.

403
00:26:19,744 --> 00:26:23,455
Little Rice Cake
is waiting for you to let her go.

404
00:26:23,456 --> 00:26:24,833
Little Rice Cake?

405
00:26:25,458 --> 00:26:26,543
Where is she?

406
00:26:33,591 --> 00:26:34,634
Li Zhuzhu,

407
00:26:35,635 --> 00:26:39,013
if you can't let go of your anger
and obsession,

408
00:26:39,014 --> 00:26:41,265
Little Rice Cake can't move on either.

409
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,559
Everyone else has gone on
to be reincarnated,

410
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:44,978
but she refuses to leave.

411
00:26:45,603 --> 00:26:49,274
Why don't you go say a proper goodbye?
Don't let her worry.

412
00:26:51,192 --> 00:26:52,694
She's right over there.

413
00:26:57,240 --> 00:26:58,366
Go.

414
00:27:10,211 --> 00:27:12,297
Go. She's waited a long time for you.

415
00:28:12,899 --> 00:28:15,860
Little Rice Cake, my baby.

416
00:28:18,613 --> 00:28:22,784
Why are you still waiting for Mommy?

417
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:33,002
I promise I'll be okay.

418
00:28:34,921 --> 00:28:40,593
Promise me you'll move on
and be reborn, okay?

419
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:24,094
- Taozi.
- What are you doing?

420
00:29:24,095 --> 00:29:26,473
Stop. I'm giving the baby back to her.

421
00:29:27,932 --> 00:29:29,017
I'm sorry.

422
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:32,604
I missed you so much.

423
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:36,857
Take good care of her,

424
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:39,652
or my husband
will send two busloads after you.

425
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:41,696
I will.

426
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:44,282
Thank you for giving Taozi back to me.

427
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:53,874
Hurry up. Walk faster.

428
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:56,960
Taozi, Ruyi, those three ghosts are here.

429
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,545
Thank you for helping us.

430
00:29:58,546 --> 00:30:00,088
- Thank you for helping us.
- Thanks.

431
00:30:00,089 --> 00:30:01,715
Taozi's back.

432
00:30:01,716 --> 00:30:03,717
Is Taozi okay?

433
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:04,844
She's fine.

434
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:06,596
Chang Ruyi,

435
00:30:07,430 --> 00:30:09,140
this is your last chance.

436
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:12,769
If you don't take good care of Taozi,
I'll take her away.

437
00:30:13,353 --> 00:30:16,438
I'll take good care of her and make sure
she grows up safe and healthy.

438
00:30:16,439 --> 00:30:19,316
Thank you.
Thank you for giving me another chance.

439
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:20,235
Thank you.

440
00:30:20,944 --> 00:30:21,945
Thank you.

441
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:24,988
All right, you three.

442
00:30:24,989 --> 00:30:27,617
You've done what you came to do.
Time to go, right?

443
00:30:29,661 --> 00:30:30,870
Auntie Pink,

444
00:30:31,621 --> 00:30:34,206
will he really go to Hell
for possessing someone?

445
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:36,333
He only did it to save Taozi.

446
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:37,584
He meant no harm.

447
00:30:37,585 --> 00:30:39,837
- He never possessed me either.
- Did I ask?

448
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:42,339
I still have things to do.
I can't let go yet.

449
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:44,258
- I heard it's scary there.
- Auntie.

450
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:46,553
Don't worry. I'll speak up for you.

451
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:51,223
Since they're leaving,

452
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:54,561
can I see them with my own eyes
and thank them?

453
00:30:58,106 --> 00:30:59,274
Can I?

454
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:01,316
She doesn't look capable.

455
00:31:01,317 --> 00:31:02,359
She's wearing pink.

456
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:04,820
Her powers can't be that strong.
She can't do it.

457
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:07,031
She's just, you know...

458
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:13,079
So that's you guys.

459
00:31:14,289 --> 00:31:15,790
Hi.

460
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:19,252
Thank you for everything
you've done for us.

461
00:31:20,211 --> 00:31:22,045
We really appreciate it.

462
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:23,214
No need to thank me.

463
00:31:23,965 --> 00:31:25,341
I hate kids anyway.

464
00:31:26,759 --> 00:31:27,593
A-Li,

465
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:30,597
if anyone ever bullies Taozi, you're dead.

466
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:32,515
And remember,

467
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:35,059
don't let anyone scare you again.

468
00:31:36,144 --> 00:31:37,186
Uncle.

469
00:31:38,271 --> 00:31:39,314
Ruyi,

470
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:42,400
I know you'll be a great mom.

471
00:31:43,234 --> 00:31:49,616
Tell little Taozi there's an auntie
who loves her very much.

472
00:31:50,533 --> 00:31:51,992
I will.

473
00:31:51,993 --> 00:31:53,243
Thanks, Auntie.

474
00:31:53,244 --> 00:31:56,246
Auntie? You're more like a great-aunt.

475
00:31:56,247 --> 00:31:57,331
You...

476
00:31:57,332 --> 00:31:58,707
Ruyi.

477
00:31:58,708 --> 00:31:59,792
Strawberry Candy.

478
00:32:03,838 --> 00:32:05,173
You're a good person.

479
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:09,636
I'm so glad I met you.

480
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:15,599
When Taozi grows up, I'll tell her about

481
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:19,646
an uncle who loved her dearly
and will always watch over her.

482
00:32:22,023 --> 00:32:23,024
Mr. Zeng,

483
00:32:23,983 --> 00:32:26,360
I'd like to hold Taozi one more time.

484
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:29,322
- Could I possess you just one last time?
- Sure, go ahead.

485
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:32,992
No possessing people.
You'll go to Hell for that.

486
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:42,377
Fine. I'll just pretend I didn't see it.

487
00:32:46,172 --> 00:32:47,590
It was nice meeting you.

488
00:32:58,309 --> 00:32:59,476
Taozi.

489
00:32:59,477 --> 00:33:00,644
Bye-bye.

490
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,396
Uncle.

491
00:33:02,397 --> 00:33:03,690
Bye-bye.

492
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:07,359
Bye-bye.

493
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:09,069
Auntie!

494
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:11,613
Miss... Auntie!

495
00:33:11,614 --> 00:33:12,657
Bye-bye.

496
00:33:14,283 --> 00:33:16,118
Stay safe, healthy, and hap...

497
00:33:16,119 --> 00:33:17,245
I will.

498
00:33:18,287 --> 00:33:19,539
A happy...

499
00:33:20,081 --> 00:33:22,542
future.

500
00:33:30,008 --> 00:33:34,261
Run, run, run! Go, go, go!

501
00:33:34,262 --> 00:33:37,014
Stay close. Are you listening?

502
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:39,808
Why so quiet? No questions?
Trying to slack off?

503
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:41,518
You're still on probation.

504
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:43,353
Being my assistant isn't easy.

505
00:33:43,354 --> 00:33:45,939
I'm not. I'm checking the equipment.

506
00:33:45,940 --> 00:33:47,649
I just rewrote the program

507
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:49,276
to improve the matching success rate.

508
00:33:49,277 --> 00:33:50,318
Did it work?

509
00:33:50,319 --> 00:33:51,738
Did we get another match?

510
00:33:55,116 --> 00:33:57,159
You were a computer engineer in life.

511
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:59,077
Those skills are really paying off now.

512
00:33:59,078 --> 00:34:01,955
The Matchmaker God
loves the matchmaking program I wrote.

513
00:34:01,956 --> 00:34:04,500
Now he won't have to make
so many random matches.

514
00:34:05,543 --> 00:34:07,794
I'll give you credit for that.

515
00:34:07,795 --> 00:34:11,174
- Thanks.
- I'd almost given up on him.

516
00:34:13,676 --> 00:34:14,801
Emergency.

517
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:17,095
Difficult labor. Let's go.

518
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:19,264
- Good luck!
- What "good luck"? You're coming too.

519
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:20,308
Quick!

520
00:34:21,267 --> 00:34:23,435
You're so brave.

521
00:34:23,436 --> 00:34:25,146
You didn't cry at all, did you?

522
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:29,274
You didn't cry during your shot, Taozi.

523
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:31,444
She probably doesn't feel much pain yet.

524
00:34:33,488 --> 00:34:34,530
Auntie.

525
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:37,867
Well...

526
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,043
Come to Mommy.

527
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:55,384
Mom, want to come in for a bit?

528
00:35:12,527 --> 00:35:14,070
- Auntie, you go first.
- Thanks.

529
00:35:24,622 --> 00:35:25,665
A-Gui.

530
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:29,042
Oh, you came too?

531
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:32,337
You finally came.
I thought you'd already been reincarnated.

532
00:35:32,338 --> 00:35:34,798
My life was so hard,
I never got to travel, you know?

533
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:38,677
So I asked the Black and White Reaper
if I could see the world.

534
00:35:38,678 --> 00:35:41,346
He's cool about it.
He said, "Have fun. Come back later."

535
00:35:41,347 --> 00:35:42,764
Thank you.

536
00:35:42,765 --> 00:35:45,977
No wonder A-Li couldn't find you.
You're always off somewhere.

537
00:35:46,602 --> 00:35:47,894
A-Li's looking for me?

538
00:35:47,895 --> 00:35:49,856
What does he want?

539
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:52,858
Always some damn problem.

540
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,360
It's not our turn yet.

541
00:36:03,828 --> 00:36:05,371
Uncle, Auntie...

542
00:36:06,414 --> 00:36:07,582
Uncle, Auntie,

543
00:36:09,041 --> 00:36:10,168
you were reincarnated.

544
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,211
Who's that?

545
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:15,881
Grandma?

546
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:19,718
Why are you such a nag?

547
00:36:19,719 --> 00:36:23,097
Grandma's already gone.
What do you want with me?

548
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:26,558
How could you do that?

549
00:36:26,559 --> 00:36:29,227
You just left without telling me anything.

550
00:36:29,228 --> 00:36:30,854
Silly boy.

551
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:34,983
I passed peacefully in my sleep.

552
00:36:34,984 --> 00:36:37,068
That's a blessing many people would envy.

553
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:41,114
And now I finally get to travel the world.

554
00:36:41,115 --> 00:36:45,619
Besides, seeing how happy you are
as a father, I can rest easy.

555
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:47,496
Me? A dad?

556
00:36:48,122 --> 00:36:51,166
I'm not a dad. Grandma, you got it wrong.

557
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:52,083
That's...

558
00:36:52,084 --> 00:36:55,337
You haven't been home,
so you don't know. It's a long story.

559
00:36:55,338 --> 00:37:00,383
Some nerd in black glasses brought
Chang Ruyi to my place.

560
00:37:00,384 --> 00:37:01,718
It's not what you think.

561
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:03,929
I just saw Taozi.

562
00:37:03,930 --> 00:37:06,933
She's exactly like you as a kid.

563
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:15,565
Thank Heaven for blessing
my silly grandson.

564
00:37:15,566 --> 00:37:18,193
You're stiff as a board
and don't even know how to date,

565
00:37:18,194 --> 00:37:24,450
yet a beautiful girl chose you
and gave you such a cute daughter.

566
00:37:26,369 --> 00:37:29,372
What? I don't get it.

567
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:31,915
You young people are crazy.

568
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:36,211
Now that you have a child,
take good care of her, okay?

569
00:37:36,212 --> 00:37:40,423
Oh, I asked the Black and White Reapers
to close your third eye,

570
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:42,426
so you won't see ghosts anymore.

571
00:37:44,470 --> 00:37:46,846
I won't see you anymore?

572
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:50,100
Silly boy. When it's time, you have to go.

573
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:54,104
No. You just came back,
and you're leaving already?

574
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:55,563
Be good. Listen to Grandma.

575
00:37:55,564 --> 00:37:57,482
No, you can't.

576
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:59,025
Listen to Grandma.

577
00:37:59,026 --> 00:38:04,990
I'll watch over your family from Heaven
and keep you all healthy.

578
00:38:04,991 --> 00:38:07,285
Bless your business. Okay?

579
00:38:10,162 --> 00:38:12,456
Be good.
Take care of your wife and daughter.

580
00:38:26,637 --> 00:38:27,722
Grandma!

581
00:38:30,808 --> 00:38:33,601
<i>You really don't know
who Taozi's father is?</i>

582
00:38:33,602 --> 00:38:34,812
A one-night stand

583
00:38:35,354 --> 00:38:36,813
at a club.

584
00:38:36,814 --> 00:38:38,107
Taozi!

585
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:41,735
<i>Here. This one's on me.</i>

586
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:43,194
- I can't drink.
- It's water.

587
00:38:43,195 --> 00:38:44,195
Water?

588
00:38:44,196 --> 00:38:47,824
Why are you so funny? You're so stiff.

589
00:38:47,825 --> 00:38:50,493
- Do you work out?
- I'm working, miss.

590
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:51,536
Let me try it on.

591
00:38:51,537 --> 00:38:54,080
- I can hear better.
- Stop playing around.

592
00:38:54,081 --> 00:38:55,915
Cheers!

593
00:38:55,916 --> 00:38:58,251
All right, all right...

594
00:38:58,252 --> 00:38:59,420
Cheers!

595
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:04,382
No, you can't.

596
00:39:04,383 --> 00:39:06,052
Who is it?

597
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:23,444
Chang Ruyi?

598
00:39:24,320 --> 00:39:26,072
There's something I need to tell you.

599
00:39:26,781 --> 00:39:27,865
What is it?

600
00:39:29,241 --> 00:39:31,035
Well...

601
00:39:32,328 --> 00:39:35,663
- How's your online business been lately?
- It's going great.

602
00:39:35,664 --> 00:39:38,000
A lot of moms support me. Why?

603
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:40,877
Do you have any suggestions?

604
00:39:40,878 --> 00:39:43,297
No. What advice could I give you?

605
00:39:44,256 --> 00:39:46,801
Whatever you decide, I'll support you.

606
00:39:49,470 --> 00:39:51,055
How would you rate me as a mom?

607
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:52,889
You?

608
00:39:52,890 --> 00:39:54,974
At least 80...

609
00:39:54,975 --> 00:39:57,228
No, 100. You're a 100-point mom.

610
00:39:59,021 --> 00:40:00,606
How could I be a perfect mom?

611
00:40:02,817 --> 00:40:06,903
I used to really want to be one,
but then I realized it's impossible.

612
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:10,281
There's so much to do.
I'm exhausted and overwhelmed.

613
00:40:10,282 --> 00:40:12,033
I need people to help me make up

614
00:40:12,034 --> 00:40:13,619
the rest of those 100 points.

615
00:40:14,703 --> 00:40:16,037
Thank you.

616
00:40:16,038 --> 00:40:17,665
Don't mention it.

617
00:40:20,376 --> 00:40:21,419
Chang Ruyi?

618
00:40:23,963 --> 00:40:25,713
I dreamed of Grandma.

619
00:40:25,714 --> 00:40:26,841
Really?

620
00:40:27,758 --> 00:40:29,926
- Didn't you always want to dream of her?
- Yeah.

621
00:40:29,927 --> 00:40:32,930
- But she told me something shocking.
- What was it?

622
00:40:34,056 --> 00:40:35,348
She said

623
00:40:35,349 --> 00:40:38,893
I'm Taozi's

624
00:40:38,894 --> 00:40:40,354
biological father.

625
00:40:41,689 --> 00:40:42,856
What?

626
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:46,151
Then I started thinking back
to around this time last year.

627
00:40:46,152 --> 00:40:48,528
There's this one night that's really hazy.

628
00:40:48,529 --> 00:40:49,988
I don't know what happened,

629
00:40:49,989 --> 00:40:53,659
but in those blurry memories,
I think I saw your face.

630
00:40:54,577 --> 00:40:59,582
And when I did the math,
the timing seemed to match.

631
00:41:00,958 --> 00:41:04,086
So I got a paternity test.

632
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:08,965
I haven't seen it yet. I haven't.

633
00:41:08,966 --> 00:41:11,343
I thought we'd look together.

634
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:14,680
Wait, I'm so nervous.

635
00:41:17,641 --> 00:41:19,350
What are you doing?

636
00:41:19,351 --> 00:41:20,603
- Chang Ruyi.
- Does it matter?

637
00:41:21,228 --> 00:41:23,354
- It doesn't matter?
- What if you're not?

638
00:41:23,355 --> 00:41:26,733
Then what? You won't love Taozi anymore?
You'll kick us out?

639
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:28,568
Of course not.

640
00:41:28,569 --> 00:41:30,904
I'll be here until...

641
00:41:30,905 --> 00:41:32,530
you don't need me anymore.

642
00:41:32,531 --> 00:41:34,158
Then it doesn't matter.

643
00:41:35,117 --> 00:41:36,452
But what if I am?

644
00:41:37,161 --> 00:41:38,369
What if you are?

645
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:39,788
Will it change anything?

646
00:41:40,789 --> 00:41:43,124
If I am, I'll propose to you.

647
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:45,793
We'll get married,
give Taozi a mom and dad,

648
00:41:45,794 --> 00:41:48,963
a loving family and plan for her future.

649
00:41:48,964 --> 00:41:50,549
- And then--
- Can't we do that anyway?

650
00:41:54,595 --> 00:41:55,763
I said if.

651
00:41:57,389 --> 00:41:58,890
- I don't know either.
- If what?

652
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:01,309
- Forget it.
- You spoke too fast. I missed it.

653
00:42:01,310 --> 00:42:03,228
I said it doesn't matter.

654
00:42:03,229 --> 00:42:05,231
What did you want to do with me?

655
00:42:06,565 --> 00:42:08,025
No, I...

656
00:42:09,026 --> 00:42:11,236
I... I don't dislike you.

657
00:42:11,237 --> 00:42:13,155
Yeah, I don't. I...

658
00:42:15,407 --> 00:42:17,076
I actually like you quite a lot.

659
00:42:19,161 --> 00:42:24,583
So, would you date me
with marriage in mind?

660
00:42:25,459 --> 00:42:27,670
Sure. I don't dislike you either.

661
00:42:28,420 --> 00:42:30,838
You're pretty strong. Great for childcare.

662
00:42:30,839 --> 00:42:34,676
You like muscular guys?
I'll work out every day. Seriously.

663
00:42:34,677 --> 00:42:36,679
- I'm fine either way.
- Either way?

664
00:42:37,388 --> 00:42:38,389
It's just...

665
00:42:42,434 --> 00:42:45,311
Taozi.

666
00:42:45,312 --> 00:42:46,772
What's wrong?

667
00:42:47,398 --> 00:42:49,024
It's <i>Baba</i> A-Li.

668
00:42:50,192 --> 00:42:51,694
Not Alibaba.

669
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,363
Be careful!

670
00:42:55,364 --> 00:42:56,699
Taozi!

671
00:42:58,909 --> 00:43:00,244
I smell poop.

672
00:43:02,830 --> 00:43:04,498
- Really? Did she poop?
- No.

673
00:43:11,380 --> 00:43:12,381
What are you looking at?

674
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:16,093
She does look like me.

675
00:43:26,353 --> 00:43:27,896
It's nothing.

676
00:43:32,776 --> 00:43:33,944
You want to know?

677
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:37,072
You tore it up.
Serves you right for acting cool.

678
00:43:48,667 --> 00:43:53,588
You two little rascals
made Mommy go through so much.

679
00:43:53,589 --> 00:43:55,966
You know how hard
it was for her now, right?

680
00:43:56,800 --> 00:44:00,220
- Was Taozi this cute?
- Of course.

681
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:04,308
Have you been secretly seeing Taozi?

682
00:44:05,017 --> 00:44:08,019
I told you, you can't.
You're different now.

683
00:44:08,020 --> 00:44:09,437
Even just one look?

684
00:44:09,438 --> 00:44:10,564
No.

685
00:44:11,065 --> 00:44:11,898
Right?

686
00:44:11,899 --> 00:44:13,066
No.

687
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:14,318
No, right?

688
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:24,369
What's wrong?

689
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:26,747
You tell me. Am I seeing this right?

690
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:32,336
You saw it right.
